   Obtain written permission; notification alone is not permission.
b. Make the complete corresponding source of the Derivative publicly
   accessible without charge when it is first distributed, deployed for
   others or otherwise made available for use, and keep it accessible for
   as long as that version is distributed or offered for use. Publish the
   source before privately using a modified version as well. This includes
   the preferred form for modification and build/install instructions,
   but excludes secrets and third-party content you lack rights to publish.
c. Apply this same source-available licence to the covered Software and
   your changes, retaining this licence, NOTICE.md and the Owner's
   attribution. You must hold the rights necessary to license your changes.
   This does not relicense excluded third-party material.
d. Inform the Owner of the public source URL and initial release, and of
   subsequent releases or a change of source location. Keep source available
   for each version still distributed or offered for use.
e. Clearly identify your modifications and their author, and do not imply
   that the Owner endorses or maintains your Derivative.

Public source is required for authorized Derivatives; it does not remove
the permission requirement for further forks or Derivatives. This is a
custom source-available licence, not an OSI-approved open-source licence.

